  "worked_solution": "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(1\\,|\\,0)=P(Y=1\\,|\\,X=0).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=1\\,|\\,X=0)=\\frac{P(X=0,Y=1)}{P(X=0)}=\\frac{f(0,1)}{{f}_{X}(0)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(0) & =f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(0,2) \\\\  & =0.3+0.2+0.1 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(0,1)=0.2.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{X}(0)=0.6$ and $f(0,1)=0.2$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(1\\,|\\,0) & =P(Y=1\\,|\\,X=0) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0,1)}{{f}_{X}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.2}{0.6} \\\\  & \u22480.33.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
